              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Cleaning Means",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Every column has the ==right dtype==",
                "No hidden ==NaN==, no duplicate rows",
                "Consistent labels and text, done {green:before} any analysis"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How It Works",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Most cleaning methods return a ==new object==",
                "The original stays untouched, so ==assign== the result"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.drop_duplicates()         # lost",
                "df = df.drop_duplicates()    # kept"
              ],
              "note": "no assignment, no cleaning"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Inspect",
                    "sub": "info, describe, isna().sum()",
