    {
      "title": "Missing Values: isna, dropna, fillna",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Missing Values: isna, dropna, fillna",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Detecting Missing",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`NaN`, `None` and `NaT` all count as ==missing==",
                "`isna()` gives a boolean mask; `notna()` is its inverse",
                "`df.isna().sum()` counts missing per column",
                "`df.isna().mean()` gives the fraction missing"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. dropna()",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Argument",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`axis=0`",
                  "drops rows"
                ],
                [
                  "`how='any'`",
                  "default: one NaN drops the row"
                ],
                [
                  "`how='all'`",
                  "drops only all-NaN rows"
                ],
                [
                  "`subset=[cols]`",
                  "checks only those columns"
                ],
                [
                  "`thresh=n`",
                  "keeps rows with ==n== or more non-null"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. fillna()",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`fillna(value)` takes a scalar or a per-column dict",
                "Standard numeric fill is the ==median==",
                "`ffill()` / `bfill()` fill from neighbours"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df['a'] = df['a'].fillna(df['a'].median())",
                "df = df.fillna({'a': 0, 'b': 'n/a'})",
                "df['a'] = df['a'].ffill()"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df[df.a == np.nan]` matches nothing: NaN == NaN is False, so use `isna()`",
                "`df['a'].fillna(x, inplace=True)` never changes df under pandas 3 Copy-on-Write"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Assign back",
              "text": "Write `df['a'] = df['a'].fillna(x)`. The result is a ==new object==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Dtypes, Conversion and Duplicates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Dtypes, Conversion and Duplicates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Reading dtypes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df.dtypes` lists the type of every column",
                "Mixed values in a column → ==object==",
                "Int column with NaN → turns {orange:float}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Converting types",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "On bad value"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`astype('int64')`",
                  "{red:raises}"
                ],
                [
                  "`astype('datetime64[ns]')`",
                  "{red:raises}"
                ],
                [
                  "`astype('category')`",
                  "never raises, every value a category"
                ],
                [
                  "`astype('Int64')`",
                  "nullable int, allows NaN (capital I)"
                ],
                [
                  "`to_numeric` / `to_datetime`",
                  "default `errors='raise'`"
                ],
                [
                  "same, `errors='coerce'`",
                  "{green:NaN / NaT}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Use ==coerce== to turn unparseable values into NaN/NaT, then inspect them"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df['age'] = pd.to_numeric(df['age'], errors='coerce')",
                "df['joined'] = pd.to_datetime(df['joined'], errors='coerce')"
              ],
              "note": "assign the result back"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Duplicates",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`duplicated()` marks repeat rows; ==keep='first'== by default, so the first copy is False",
                "`drop_duplicates(subset=[cols], keep='first'|'last'|False)` removes them",
                "`keep=False` drops **every** copy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df.duplicated().sum()",
                "df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=['email'], keep='last')"
              ],
              "note": "count first, then drop"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Near-duplicates survive",
              "text": "With no `subset`, all columns are compared, so 'Ann' and ' ann ' stay. ==Clean text first==, then dedupe."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "String Methods and Renaming",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "String Methods and Renaming",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The .str Accessor",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`.str` applies string methods to a whole ==Series==",
                "`strip()` `lower()` `upper()` `title()` `len()`",
                "`replace('old','new', regex=False)` = literal; `regex=True` = patterns",
                "`contains('x', na=False)` = boolean mask",
                "`split(',', expand=True)` = separate columns"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "s.str.strip().str.title()",
                "s.str.replace(r'\\s+', ' ', regex=True)",
                "df[s.str.contains('x', na=False)]",
                "s.str.split(',', expand=True)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Renaming",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Form",
                "Renames",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`rename(columns={'old':'new'})`",
                  "chosen columns",
                  "copy"
                ],
                [
                  "`df.columns = [...]`",
                  "all; count must match",
                  "in place"
                ],
                [
                  "`rename(columns=str.lower)`",
                  "every name",
                  "copy"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`.str` on a non-string column raises ==AttributeError==",
                "Missing values return NaN, no error"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fix",
              "text": "Convert first: `astype('string')`"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Does rename change df?** No, it returns a copy; assign it back.",
                "**Why does .str fail?** The dtype is not string; use `astype('string')`."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Apply vs Vectorized Operations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Apply vs Vectorized Operations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Speed Ladder",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Pattern",
                "Python calls",
                "Speed"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`df['a'] * 2`, `s.str.lower()`, `np.where`",
                  "none, compiled column-wide",
                  "{green:fastest}"
                ],
                [
                  "`map(dict)`",
                  "fast lookup",
                  "fast"
                ],
                [
                  "`Series.apply(func)`",
                  "once per element",
                  "slow"
                ],
                [
                  "`df.apply(func, axis=1)`",
                  "once per row",
                  "{red:slowest}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing and Replacing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==apply== only when no vectorized form exists, e.g. multi-step custom logic",
                "`map(dict)` recodes values by lookup",
                "Replace row-wise if/else with `np.where` or a boolean mask"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "df['tier'] = np.where(df.score >= 50, 'pass', 'fail')",
                "df['city'] = df['code'].map({'H': 'Hyd', 'B': 'Blr'})"
              ],
              "note": "vectorized if/else and dict recode"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Slow apply",
              "text": "`df.apply(f, axis=1)` on a large frame is often **10 to 100 times** slower than the vectorized form."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Default `axis=0` passes whole ==columns==, not rows",
                "**Why is axis=1 slowest?** One Python call per row",
                "**What replaces row-wise if/else?** `np.where` or a mask"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
